WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士们。

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.900
Hello, Angela.
你好，安吉拉。

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.560
Hey, lady.
嘿，女士。

10
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.500
It's very good to see your face today.
今天见到你真高兴。

11
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.300
Same.
我也是。

12
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.560
I feel the same way.
我有同感。

13
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.740
Oh, I said lady right out of the gate.
噢，我一开口就说了“女士”。

14
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.460
Jenna, some people love the lady and some people don't love the lady.
珍娜，有些人喜欢这个称呼，有些人不喜欢。

15
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.420
I get a t-shirt that just says lady.
我甚至收到了一件印着“女士”字样的T恤。

16
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:44.440
Lady.
女士。

17
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:45.720
All right.
好吧。

18
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.680
What are we talking about today?
我们今天聊什么？

19
00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:53.240
Today, we are talking about Season 3, Episode 18, The Negotiation.
今天我们要聊的是第三季第十八集《谈判》。

20
00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:54.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

21
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.880
It was written by Mike Schur and directed by Jeff Blitz.
这一集由迈克·舒尔编剧，杰夫·布里茨执导。

22
00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.300
Those are two powerhouses of comedy.
他们俩可是喜剧界的重量级人物。

23
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.020
Yes, this is a good team.
没错，这是个强强联手的组合。

24
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.720
Here is a summary.
以下是剧情梗概。

25
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:13.620
Angered by Pam's confession that she and Jim shared a kiss, Roy tries to attack Jim in the office.
帕姆坦白了她和吉姆曾接吻过，罗伊因此大发雷霆，试图在办公室袭击吉姆。

26
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.580
I mean, right out of the gate.
我是说，一开场就是这样。

27
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.840
That's the first scene, everybody.
大家注意，这就是第一场戏。

28
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:17.580
Yeah.
没错。

29
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.460
Jim is spared by Dwight's quick thinking, a.k.a.
多亏了德怀特反应迅速，也就是所谓的……

30
00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.280
pepper spray.
防狼喷雾，吉姆才幸免于难。

31
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:27.840
Roy is fired and Daryl tries to leverage it into a raise.
罗伊被解雇了，达里尔试图借此机会要求加薪。

32
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:37.780
But upon hearing how little Michael makes at his job, Daryl, Toby, and Michael drive to corporate so Michael can ask for his own raise.
但在得知迈克尔的薪水竟然那么低后，达里尔、托比和迈克尔开车前往公司总部，好让迈克尔去争取他自己的加薪。

33
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.620
Roy takes Pam out for coffee to apologize, and they break it off for good.
罗伊约帕姆出去喝咖啡道歉，他们彻底分手了。

34
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:44.900
This is it.
就是这样。

35
00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.100
No more Pam and Roy, guys.
伙计们，帕姆和罗伊彻底结束了。

36
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:54.040
And then at the end of the show, Jim catches Dwight and Angela kissing in the office.
然后在剧集结尾，吉姆撞见德怀特和安吉拉在办公室接吻。

37
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

38
00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:57.440
It's a lot.
信息量很大。

39
00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:58.960
It's a lot.
确实很大。

40
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:04.220
Fast fact number one, this episode was a supersized episode of The Office.
第一个速览事实，这一集是《办公室》的超长集。

41
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.860
And as a result, Angela, I think, am I right?
所以，安吉拉，我想，我说得对吗？

42
00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.440
There are no deleted scenes for this episode.
这一集没有删减片段。

43
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.300
There are none on the DVDs.
DVD里一个都没有。

44
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:19.940
Now, I don't know if there's some secret NBC archive somewhere, but there aren't any that we know of.
我不确定NBC某个地方是否藏着秘密档案，但据我们所知，确实没有。

45
00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.500
I think we used it all.
我想我们把素材都用上了。

46
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.800
It's all in there, guys.
伙计们，全都在正片里了。

47
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.600
Now, here's a little bit of a fact.
现在，这里有个小事实。

48
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.560
This is a fact within a fact.
这是一个事实中的事实。

49
00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.200
I was going to say, a little bit of a fact.
我正想说呢，一个小事实。

50
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.060
What's happening?
怎么了？

51
00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:38.600
This episode, like I said, was written by Mike Schur, who was nominated for an Emmy Award for writing this episode.
正如我所说，这一集是由迈克·舒尔编写的，他凭借这一集的剧本获得了艾美奖提名。

52
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.420
Oh, he should have won.
噢，他本该获奖的。

53
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.480
Did he win?
他获奖了吗？

54
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.640
He did not.
没有。

55
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:43.820
Oh, boo.
噢，真可惜。

56
00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.060
He lost to Greg Daniels, who won for Gay Witch Hunt.
他输给了格雷格·丹尼尔斯，后者凭借《同性恋女巫狩猎》那一集拿了奖。

57
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.160
Oh, okay.
噢，好吧。

58
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:49.560
Okay.
好吧。

59
00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:49.860
Okay.
好吧。

60
00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.380
You're all right with that.
你对此没意见吧。

61
00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.100
You're like, all right.
你觉得，还行吧。

62
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.280
The Office won.
是《办公室》赢了。

63
00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.840
Keep it in the family.
肥水不流外人田嘛。

64
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:56.580
That's right.
没错。

65
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:57.480
Yay.
耶。

66
00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:58.420
All right.
好吧。

67
00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.480
Well, that was fun.
嗯，这很有趣。

68
00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.380
All right.
好吧。

69
00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.420
Well, now I'm going to give you fast fact number two.
好了，现在我要告诉你们第二个冷知识。

70
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:09.820
So, in this episode, you remember Michael says that he got tips on how to negotiate from Wikipedia.
在这一集中，你们记得迈克尔说他从维基百科上学到了谈判技巧吗？

71
00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:10.920
Yes.
记得。

72
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:21.220
And some of the stuff that he says that he found on Wikipedia is stuff like, you have to suddenly change the location or refuse to talk firSt.
他提到的一些从维基百科上看到的内容，比如必须突然改变地点，或者拒绝先开口说话。

73
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.360
Yes.
是的。

74
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:33.340
Well, we had a fan question from Brianna Kernan, Zhu Yu Wang, Charlie Altman, Shea Quiz, and Jeremy Sharp.
我们收到了来自布里安娜·克南、朱玉王（音译）、查理·奥特曼、谢伊·奎兹和杰里米·夏普的粉丝提问。

75
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:42.280
They all asked, were the interview tips that Michael was using actually from Wikipedia or did the writers make them up?
他们都问，迈克尔用的那些面试技巧真的是来自维基百科，还是编剧们编出来的？

76
00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:43.660
Okay.
好的。

77
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.420
None of that stuff was on Wikipedia.
那些内容根本不在维基百科上。

78
00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.600
For real.
真的吗？

79
00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.600
For real.
真的。

80
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.020
The writers just made that up.
那是编剧们瞎编的。

81
00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.000
Yeah.
是啊。

82
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:56.240
I, you know, Jenna, I did a mini deep dive on the art of negotiation for this episode.
你知道吗，珍娜，我为了这一集专门对谈判艺术做了一次小型深度挖掘。

83
00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:02.980
And I can confirm because I went to the actual Wikipedia page for negotiating and those are not on there.
我可以确认，因为我查了维基百科上关于“谈判”的实际页面，上面并没有那些内容。

84
00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:09.220
Well, you know, after this episode aired, there was a major stir.
嗯，你知道吗，这一集播出后，引起了不小的轰动。

85
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:10.820
Really?
真的吗？

86
00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:11.860
Really?
真的吗？

87
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:20.320
And then the administration started going onto the negotiation page of Wikipedia and they started changing it to reflect Michael's advice.
然后维基百科的管理员开始进入谈判页面，并开始修改它，以反映迈克尔的建议。

88
00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.760
That's awesome.
太棒了。

89
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.060
I mean, not, I mean, don't, don't be hackers, guys, but that's funny.
我是说，别，大家别去当黑客，但这确实很有趣。

90
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:34.340
And the administrators at Wikipedia had to put the page in, I guess, what is called semi-protection mode.
维基百科的管理员不得不把那个页面设为，我想应该是叫“半保护模式”。

91
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.380
And that limits who's allowed to edit a page.
那会限制谁有权编辑页面。

92
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:49.480
So any user that had an account that was less than four days old or anyone who's trying to put a post up as anonymous were forbidden.
所以任何注册时间少于四天的用户，或者任何试图以匿名身份发帖的人都被禁止了。

93
00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:59.600
And then they had other administrators who would go in and delete all of the fake negotiation advice that was just Michael Scott.
然后还有其他管理员会进去删除所有那些纯属迈克尔·斯科特式的虚假谈判建议。

94
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.260
Oh, my goodness, you guys.
天哪，伙计们。

95
00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.080
But it was a whole thing.
这真是一场大风波。

96
00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.180
There were like articles written about it in USA Today.
《今日美国》甚至还为此写了报道。

97
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:08.900
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

98
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:09.480
Yeah.
是啊。

99
00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.600
It caused a stir.
这引起了轰动。

100
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.540
Stirring it up, office fans.
《办公室》的粉丝们，真是闹得沸沸扬扬啊。

101
00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.060
I'm going through these quickly, Angela, because we have some exciting news, which is part of Fast Fact No.
安吉拉，我得快点过一遍这些内容，因为我们有个令人兴奋的消息，属于“快速事实”第

102
00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:18.380
3.
3条。

103
00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.280
Yes.
没错。

104
00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.480
This episode marks the return of Ed Helms as Andy Bernard.
这一集标志着艾德·赫尔姆斯饰演的安迪·伯纳德回归。

105
00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:31.880
But it also marks the last regular appearance of Roy, played by David Denman.
但也标志着大卫·丹曼饰演的罗伊最后一次作为常规角色出现。

106
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:38.620
Now, Roy will continue to come back now and then, but this really officially ends the Pam-Roy relationship.
虽然罗伊之后还会偶尔回来，但这确实正式终结了帕姆和罗伊的关系。

107
00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:45.580
And we felt like we had to mark this occasion by talking to Roy himself, David Denman.
我们觉得必须通过采访罗伊本人——大卫·丹曼，来纪念这一时刻。

108
00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.220
And we had so much fun talking to him.
我们和他聊得非常开心。

109
00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.100
Sam, can you play that interview?
山姆，能播放那段采访吗？

110
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:55.450
David Denman, hello.
大卫·丹曼，你好。

111
00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.770
Welcome to Office, ladies.
欢迎来到《办公室》，女士们。

112
00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.330
Hello, ladies.
你好，女士们。

113
00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.530
Hey, David.
嘿，大卫。

114
00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:00.890
It's so good to see you.
见到你真好。

115
00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:01.910
Been a long time.
好久不见了。

116
00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.490
Yeah, it's been a long time.
是啊，好久不见。

117
00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:04.150
It has.
确实。

118
00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:11.270
Well, David, we always like to start by asking our guests how they came to be on the show.
大卫，我们总是喜欢先问嘉宾是怎么加入这部剧的。

119
00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:18.390
My buddy, who is an actor, a friend of mine in New York, he watched The British Office.
我有个哥们儿，也是个演员，在纽约，他看过英版《办公室》。

120
00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:22.210
And he called me and said, dude, you've got to watch the show.
他打电话给我说，老兄，你一定要看这部剧。

121
00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.210
It's amazing.
太棒了。

122
00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:25.470
You're going to love it.
你一定会喜欢的。

123
00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.810
There's nothing like it on TV.
电视上从没见过这样的剧。

124
00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.790
And I hear they're doing an American version.
而且我听说他们要拍美版了。

125
00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.790
You've got to try to get in on that.
你一定要想办法争取个角色。

126
00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.290
So I watched it and I was like, oh, my God, this is genius.
所以我看了，当时就觉得，天哪，这简直是天才之作。

127
00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:38.310
And there was, you know, a couple of guys my age on the show.
而且你知道，剧里有几个和我年纪相仿的家伙。

128
00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.390
And I called my agent.
于是我给经纪人打了电话。

129
00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:43.690
I was like, hey, I hear they're doing an American version of The Office.
我说，嘿，我听说他们要拍美版《办公室》了。

130
00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.890
And he goes, yeah, yeah.
他说，是啊，没错。

131
00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.370
And I go, I'd love to get in on that.
我说，我很想参与其中。

132
00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.550
And he goes, really?
他说，真的吗？

133
00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.710
You want to do that?
你想演那个？

134
00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.270
I go, yeah.
我说，是啊。

135
00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:53.170
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

136
00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.470
Because I don't know.
因为我不知道啊。

137
00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.190
They're looking for improv comedians.
他们正在找即兴喜剧演员。

138
00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:57.670
And I'm like, yeah.
我说，没错。

139
00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.430
You know, I went to Juilliard.
你知道，我可是茱莉亚学院毕业的。

140
00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.230
I did study improv along with Shakespeare and many other things.
我学过即兴表演，还有莎士比亚戏剧以及其他很多东西。

141
00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.810
It's not just because I didn't go to, you know, ImprovOlympic or whatever.
不能因为我没去过什么即兴奥林匹克之类的学校，

142
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:12.050
It doesn't mean I don't have an interest in that and don't have that in my toolbox.
就代表我对那方面没兴趣，或者我没掌握那项技能。

143
00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:12.830
And he goes, oh, OK.
他说，哦，好吧。

144
00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.690
So he called over and all the parts were cast except for Roy.
于是他打了个电话过去，当时除了罗伊，所有角色都定下来了。

145
00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.770
And so I said, yeah, I'd love to go in for that part.
所以我说，好，我很乐意去试那个角色。

146
00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.410
That little thing changed my career.
那件小事改变了我的职业生涯。

147
00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:27.090
Well, David, I remember that you were one of the very, very first people caSt.
大卫，我记得你是最早、最早被选中的演员之一。

148
00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.530
You were at our first original table read that Angela was not even at.
你参加了我们第一次剧本围读，当时安吉拉甚至还没在场。

149
00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.610
They hadn't even filled out the rest of The Office.
那时他们甚至还没把《办公室》的其他角色填满。

150
00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:43.310
It was just Steve, John, Rain, BJ, me, Phyllis, and you.
当时只有史蒂夫、约翰、雷恩、B.J.、我、菲利斯和你。

151
00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.390
That's who was at the first table read.
那就是第一次剧本围读时在场的人。

152
00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:53.490
And I remember Alison Jones brought her Polaroid camera and she took a Polaroid picture for each
我记得艾莉森·琼斯带了她的拍立得相机，她给我们要拍的每个人都拍了一张照片，

153
00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:58.570
of us because she said that's a tradition of hers at table reads for actors at their
因为她说这是她的一种传统，在演员第一次参加剧本围读时，

154
00:07:58.570 --> 00:07:59.910
for their first series.
为他们的第一部剧集留念。

155
00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.470
Do you still have yours?
你还留着你的那张吗？

156
00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.530
I remember it slightly different.
我的记忆稍微有点不同。

157
00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:09.390
I know she brought the Polaroid camera and she took a picture for herself that she did
我知道她带了拍立得相机，也确实给自己拍了一张，这是她

158
00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.610
on every table read of her first show.
在每部剧的第一次围读时都会做的。

159
00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.650
And you said, oh, I want one of those.
然后你说，哦，我也想要一张。

160
00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.610
She took another one and gave it to you.
她就又拍了一张给了你。

161
00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:18.990
I don't think anyone else has any of those photos besides those two.
我觉得除了你们俩，没别人有那些照片了。

162
00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.910
Okay, that sounds like me.
好吧，这听起来确实像是我会做的事。

163
00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.410
Thank you, David, because Jenna has talked about this.
谢谢你，大卫，因为珍娜一直都在说这件事。

164
00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.670
And thank you for setting that straight.
谢谢你把事实澄清了。

165
00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.050
Well, that explains why no one else has one but me.
好吧，这下解释了为什么除了我之外没人有照片了。

166
00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.590
Yeah.
是啊。

167
00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:40.330
Maybe you should stop asking that question, Jenna, to the original table read people.
也许你不该再问那个问题了，珍娜，问那些最初参加围读的人。

168
00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.390
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

169
00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:46.850
Well, David, I just remember meeting you and being so excited.
好吧，大卫，我只记得见到你时特别兴奋。

170
00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.310
And we had that theater connection because I also got a theater degree.
而且我们有戏剧方面的共同点，因为我也拿到了戏剧学位。

171
00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.650
I just liked you immediately.
我当时就立刻喜欢上你了。

172
00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.370
I immediately liked you.
我立刻就喜欢上你了。

173
00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.010
No, we definitely hit it off.
不，我们确实一见如故。

174
00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:02.230
It was what was fun about that show in the beginning was you guys were all stuck in the
那部剧最有趣的地方在于，起初你们所有人都被困在

175
00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:05.510
office for hours and hours and hours.
办公室里，一待就是好几个小时。

176
00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:09.310
And usually when you film a series, it's like, oh, we'll shoot that scene and then we'll go
通常拍电视剧时，大家会想，哦，我们要拍那场戏，然后去

177
00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.110
shoot that scene.
拍那场戏。

178
00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:14.390
But because the way they filmed this with, you know, a documentary style where they whipped
但因为他们拍摄的方式，你知道，那种纪录片风格，他们需要把

179
00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:19.310
the camera across the whole office, they needed everyone to sit in the background all day
摄像机在整个办公室扫来扫去，所以他们需要每个人整天都坐在背景里。

180
00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:19.630
long.
长。

181
00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:24.070
So you guys would always be losing your mind by the time I showed up on set.
所以每次我到片场时，你们都已经快疯了。

182
00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.670
You were like, oh, there's a new person.
你们会说，哦，来新人了。

183
00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:27.470
Hi.
嗨。

184
00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:31.330
And you were very enthusiastic every time I got there.
每次我到那儿，你们都表现得非常热情。

185
00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.310
And I was very grateful for it.
我对此非常感激。

186
00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.050
You know, so, yeah, we definitely hit it off.
所以，是的，我们确实一见如故。

187
00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.690
I do remember Jenna coming to set, though, and being like, guess what I did this weekend?
不过我确实记得珍娜来片场时会说，猜猜我周末干嘛了？

188
00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:39.230
I was like, what?
我会问，干嘛了？

189
00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.070
And she was like, I played poker with David.
她说，我和大卫打扑克去了。

190
00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.630
And I was like, what is happening?
我就想，这是什么情况？

191
00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:43.750
Where are you guys?
你们在哪儿呢？

192
00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:44.910
You guys are like hanging out.
你们竟然私下聚会。

193
00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.430
You're playing poker in someone's garage.
在某人的车库里打扑克。

194
00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.270
Like, what's this whole other life I need to get in on?
就像是，我错过了什么样的新生活？

195
00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.070
I know you never learned poker, Angela.
我知道你从来没学过扑克，安吉拉。

196
00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.470
You missed out on a lot.
你错过了很多乐趣。

197
00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.850
Well, you wouldn't want me at your poker table.
好吧，你肯定不会想让我上你的牌桌的。

198
00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:00.990
I mean, I mean, one time I played with and I had like a pair of threes and I thought I
我是说，有一次我玩的时候，我手里有一对三，我以为

199
00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:01.970
could win the whole thing.
我能赢下整场比赛。

200
00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:03.970
But I guess that's not, you know, I don't know.
但我想那并不是，你知道，我也不太懂。

201
00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:04.870
I'm not good at it, guys.
伙计们，我不擅长这个。

202
00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:08.210
Well, if we're playing for real money, we would want you at our poker table.
嗯，如果我们玩真钱的话，我们肯定想让你坐在我们的牌桌上。

203
00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:12.170
No, you wouldn't because I'm the person that's like, all in.
不，你们不会想的，因为我是那种直接全押的人。

204
00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:13.730
And everyone's like, wait, what's happening?
然后大家都会想，等等，发生什么事了？

205
00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:20.810
I remember that like in Rain's garage, like, and here we are in a little poker table.
我记得那是在雷恩的车库里，就像现在我们坐在这张小牌桌旁一样。

206
00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:28.370
But I remember I took down a big pot opposite you, Jenna, once and you lost your mind.
但我记得有一次我赢了你一大笔筹码，珍娜，你当时都快疯了。

207
00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.970
You could not believe that I had beat you in that hand.
你简直不敢相信在那局牌里我竟然赢了你。

208
00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.250
I don't think I ever won another hand against you.
我觉得我之后再也没赢过你一局。

209
00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:39.530
But that one just set the time you were just so livid that I'd beat you.
但那一次真的让我印象深刻，你当时因为我赢了你而气急败坏。

210
00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:40.670
And do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

211
00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.690
Or that's just my fond memory?
还是说这只是我美好的回忆？

212
00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:47.690
I feel like I would often get dramatic when I lost and wasn't expecting it.
我觉得我输牌的时候经常会表现得很戏剧化，尤其是当我没预料到会输的时候。

213
00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:54.030
So, David, Jenna and I have talked a little bit how we give our characters backstories.
所以，大卫，珍娜和我聊过一点关于我们如何为角色设定背景故事的事。

214
00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:57.750
Like, I would give Angela Martin reasons why she would react one way.
比如，我会给安吉拉·马丁设定她为什么会那样反应的理由。

215
00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:59.670
And Jenna has shared her Pam backstory.
珍娜也分享过她对帕姆的背景设定。

216
00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.850
And what was your take on Roy and Pam?
那你对罗伊和帕姆是怎么看的？

217
00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.290
Did you invent a backstory for their relationship and for Roy?
你有没有为他们的关系和罗伊这个角色构思过背景故事？

218
00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.470
Yeah, I did definitely have backstory.
是的，我确实有背景设定。

219
00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:20.310
But I just, you know, I assumed that these guys met in high school, they started dating and, you know, they just kind of fell into this, you know,
但我只是，你知道，我假设他们是在高中认识的，开始约会，然后，你知道，他们就陷入了这种，你知道，

220
00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:27.930
this dynamic where neither one of them, well, definitely, I don't even think Roy wanted to, you know, get married initially.
这种状态，他们俩谁都没想过，嗯，我甚至觉得罗伊起初根本不想结婚。

221
00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.350
I think it was just like, oh, this is what we're supposed to do next and this is what we're supposed to do next.
我觉得他只是觉得，哦，这是我们接下来该做的事，然后又是下一件该做的事。

222
00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:41.710
And it wasn't until years later that, like, you know, when he was going to lose Pam that, like, he was like, oh,
直到多年以后，当他快要失去帕姆的时候，他才意识到，哦，

223
00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:44.690
I actually care about this person and I have to put some work into this.
我其实很在乎这个人，我必须为这段关系付出努力。

224
00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:49.390
And, you know, with any relationship, you have to put some effort into it.
而且，你知道，任何关系都需要你付出努力。

225
00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:55.630
And I don't think, I don't think Roy was, had ever thought about that until it was too late.
我不觉得，我不觉得罗伊曾经考虑过这一点，直到为时已晚。

226
00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:04.310
And I went to a school with a bunch, with some, like, couple of meatheads that I sort of fashioned this guy after.
我上学时认识一群，或者说几个，那种四肢发达头脑简单的家伙，我就是照着他们的样子塑造了这个角色。

227
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:09.290
I mean, I'm not going to say who they were, but that's kind of where I saw Roy.
我是说，我不会说他们是谁，但那就是我眼中罗伊的样子。

228
00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.490
And so I thought at the time, I was like, oh, this will be a great way to make fun of those guys.
当时我还想，哦，这会是嘲讽那些家伙的好方法。

229
00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:16.810
And then the next thing I know, I'm playing these parts for the rest of my life.
结果没想到，我余生都在扮演这类角色。

230
00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.230
That's not all.
不止这些。

231
00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.170
That's not entirely true.
那也不完全对。

232
00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:29.770
Well, it's so funny because you, I mean, like, knowing you, you're such, like, more of, like, an intellectual creative.
嗯，这很有趣，因为你，我是说，了解你的人都知道，你其实更像是一个知识分子型的创作者。

233
00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:31.810
Right?
对吧？

234
00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.130
Thank you.
谢谢。

235
00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.050
I appreciate that.
我很感激。

236
00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.610
You're an outdoorsman, though.
不过你确实是个户外运动爱好者。

237
00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:38.770
Like, that part of Roy fits you, I think.
我觉得罗伊的那一部分和你很像。

238
00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:43.990
Like, I mean, Roy is jet skiing, but, you know, you like the outdoors and stuff.
我是说，罗伊会去玩水上摩托，但你知道，你也喜欢户外活动之类的。

239
00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:45.390
I do.
我是喜欢。

240
00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.430
I do like the outdoors.
我确实喜欢户外活动。

241
00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:49.130
I mean, I go, I go out backpacking and stuff like that.
我是说，我会去背包旅行之类的。

242
00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:50.550
I don't know if Roy is necessarily that.
我不确定罗伊是不是那种人。

243
00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:55.690
He's more of like a, let's get my RV and my jet ski and, like, hang out and drink some beers.
他更像是那种，开着房车，带着水上摩托，然后聚在一起喝啤酒的人。

244
00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:56.150
Yeah.
没错。

245
00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:58.990
And, and that's his, that's his outdoorsman.
那才是他的户外生活方式。

246
00:12:59.330 --> 00:12:59.610
Right.
对。

247
00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:02.090
He's going to load up a four-wheeler with a bunch of beer.
他会往四轮摩托车上装满啤酒。

248
00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:02.550
Exactly.
没错。

249
00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:17.750
Too, how you can kind of fall into a casting rut because I just did an interview yesterday and the person interviewing me said, so, Angela, you often play the heel.
关于你怎么会陷入某种角色类型化的困境，因为我昨天刚做了一个采访，采访我的人说，安吉拉，你经常扮演反派角色。

250
00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.090
You're kind of a heel in everything.
你在每部戏里好像都是个反派。

251
00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:28.370
And I was like, yes, I, I have sort of made a way of playing the bitch or the weirdo.
当时我就想，是的，我，我算是找到了一种扮演泼妇或怪胎的方法。

252
00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.010
It's kind of become my thing.
这已经成了我的招牌了。

253
00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:34.950
It's hard for people to see you outside of that box once you're in it.
一旦你被贴上那种标签，人们就很难再用别的眼光看你了。

254
00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:40.770
And, and then like the success of the show has just continued on and on and on and on, which is fantastic.
而且，后来这部剧的成功一直持续，持续，持续，持续下去，这真是太棒了。

255
00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.210
It's more popular now than it ever was.
它现在比以往任何时候都更受欢迎。

256
00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:53.930
And, you know, if you're lucky enough to be part of something that like people enjoy and get into, and that's exciting.
而且，你知道，如果你足够幸运，能参与到一部人们喜欢并沉浸其中的作品中，那是非常令人兴奋的。

257
00:13:54.070 --> 00:14:03.250
But when you, to be part of something that gets into the culture of, that is so rare and so impossible to, to be a part of that.
但当你参与的作品能够深入文化层面时，那是非常罕见且几乎不可能实现的。

258
00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:08.490
I'm constantly grateful every day that I got to be in a little part, part of the show.
我每天都不断地心怀感激，因为我能在这部剧中占有一席之地。

259
00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:12.230
Cause that's, you know, very, very, very rare.
因为那，你知道，是非常、非常、非常罕见的。

260
00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:12.770
Yeah.
是的。

261
00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:20.230
So David, at the beginning of season three, you came back to work and you were like super fit.
那么大卫，在第三季开始时，你回来工作时看起来超级健壮。

262
00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:21.690
We all noticed.
我们都注意到了。

263
00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:27.470
Was this because you had done a movie role over the summer and they wrote it into the plot?
这是因为你夏天拍了一部电影，然后他们把这个情节写进剧本了吗？

264
00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:37.090
Or did Greg get you aside and tell you this idea that Roy should come back and be all like excited to win Pam back?
还是格雷格把你拉到一边，告诉你罗伊应该回来，并且表现出想要赢回帕姆的决心？

265
00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.270
And you sort of transformed for the show.
然后你为了这部剧进行了蜕变。

266
00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:43.010
It was all for the show, but it was, and it was a conversation with Greg.
这确实全是为了这部剧，但这是我和格雷格的一次谈话。

267
00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.870
I wouldn't say Greg said, Hey, go get in shape.
我不会说格雷格当时说，嘿，去锻炼身体吧。

268
00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:57.390
But he did say, um, he did take me aside and said, Hey, uh, I want, I got the, I'd like to make you more of a rival, uh, Jim's next season.
但他确实说，嗯，他确实把我拉到一边说，嘿，我想，我有个想法，我想让你在下一季成为吉姆更有力的竞争对手。

269
00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:58.530
And I said, really?
我说，真的吗？

270
00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.130
And he goes, yeah.
他说，是的。

271
00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.970
I said, I don't know how we're going to do that.
我说，我不知道我们要怎么做到这一点。

272
00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.870
I mean, we've really made this guy such a knucklehead.
我的意思是，我们已经把这个角色塑造成了一个十足的笨蛋。

273
00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.810
I don't know how anyone's going to root for Roy.
我不知道还有谁会支持罗伊。

274
00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:15.630
And he goes, well, I think, I think, I think you can do something and make it work when we, we can also, you know, write it.
他说，嗯，我想，我想，我想你可以做点什么让它奏效，而且我们也可以，你知道，把它写进剧本里。

275
00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.070
And so, so we, we give them that opportunity.
所以，所以我们，我们给了他们那个机会。

276
00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.730
And, uh, I said, okay.
然后，我说了，好吧。

277
00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:22.830
I said, well, I probably should get into shape then.
我说，那我也许应该去锻炼一下身体了。

278
00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.790
He goes, okay, if you want to.
他说，好吧，如果你想的话。

279
00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:34.050
And one of our camera operators who became a director, you know, our buddy, Matt Soan, um, he was like, you should do the, this triathlon.
我们的一位后来成为导演的摄影师，你知道，我们的好哥们马特·索恩，他当时说，你应该参加这个铁人三项。

280
00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.450
And I was like, are you out of your mind?
我当时就说，你疯了吗？

281
00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.550
I'm not doing a triathlon.
我才不参加什么铁人三项。

282
00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.910
I don't even, I, I barely run.
