Oh, oh, wait.
哦，等等。

1355
01:02:41.850 --> 01:02:42.910
Surf's up, bruh.
冲浪去咯，兄弟。

1356
01:02:43.350 --> 01:02:43.770
Yes.
没错。

1357
01:02:44.290 --> 01:02:45.230
Johnny Utah.
强尼·犹他。

1358
01:02:45.570 --> 01:02:46.410
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1359
01:02:46.710 --> 01:02:48.170
Let me tell you this.
我跟你说。

1360
01:02:48.550 --> 01:02:52.710
You thought that Speed was peak Keanu Reeves hotness.
你以为《生死时速》是基努·里维斯的颜值巅峰。

1361
01:02:53.030 --> 01:02:58.370
But in Point Break, he starts in the rain and he ends in the rain.
但在《惊爆点》里，他从雨中开始，又在雨中结束。

1362
01:02:58.650 --> 01:02:59.030
Okay.
好吧。

1363
01:02:59.110 --> 01:03:04.730
He's, it's a beautiful, it, Catherine Bigelow directed it.
那部电影太美了，是凯瑟琳·毕格罗执导的。

1364
01:03:05.090 --> 01:03:05.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1365
01:03:05.650 --> 01:03:08.590
Again, there is in the movie Point Break,
再说一次，在《惊爆点》这部电影里，

1366
01:03:08.590 --> 01:03:16.370
there is a five minute, at least five minute foot chase through people's backyards and houses
有一场长达五分钟，至少五分钟的追逐戏，穿过人们的后院和房子，

1367
01:03:16.370 --> 01:03:18.130
and jumping over fences.
还要跳过栅栏。

1368
01:03:18.730 --> 01:03:20.670
When do you see that anymore in movies?
现在在电影里你还能看到这种镜头吗？

1369
01:03:20.670 --> 01:03:22.810
I absolutely love both these movies.
我绝对爱死这两部电影了。

1370
01:03:22.810 --> 01:03:31.930
So I have decided that to get me through the rest of 2020, I will become a Keanu Reeves film
所以我决定，为了撑过2020年剩下的日子，我要成为一名基努·里维斯电影

1371
01:03:31.930 --> 01:03:32.650
aficionado.
爱好者。

1372
01:03:32.910 --> 01:03:36.950
And I think I'm going to start next on the John Wick movies, which I've never seen.
我想我接下来要看《疾速追杀》系列，我还没看过呢。

1373
01:03:37.930 --> 01:03:40.210
Well, Josh has seen the John Wick movies.
乔什看过《疾速追杀》系列。

1374
01:03:40.790 --> 01:03:44.970
He told me they might be too violent for me, but I love Keanu Reeves.
他跟我说那对我来说可能太暴力了，但我爱基努·里维斯。

1375
01:03:45.070 --> 01:03:46.090
You know, I love him.
你知道的，我爱他。

1376
01:03:46.170 --> 01:03:46.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1377
01:03:46.950 --> 01:03:50.670
And I have seen pretty much all of his movies, but maybe I'll watch John Wick with you.
我几乎看过他所有的电影，但也许我会和你一起看《疾速追杀》。

1378
01:03:50.850 --> 01:03:53.310
Let's watch John Wick and we'll get back to each other.
我们一起看《疾速追杀》，然后再交流一下。

1379
01:03:53.750 --> 01:03:56.210
We're going to have to go into some Bill and Ted's.
我们还得看点《比尔和泰德》系列。

1380
01:03:56.350 --> 01:03:57.670
You know, the new one just came out.
你知道，新的一部刚上映。

1381
01:03:57.670 --> 01:04:02.090
And my friend Aaron Hayes got to kiss Keanu Reeves.
而且我的朋友亚伦·海耶斯还亲过基努·里维斯。

1382
01:04:02.530 --> 01:04:06.010
Well, you're going to need to get some information on that and bring that to the podcaSt.
好吧，你得打听点内幕，然后在播客里分享一下。

1383
01:04:06.570 --> 01:04:09.190
Aaron was in Hot Wives of Vegas with me on Hulu.
亚伦和我一起演过Hulu的《拉斯维加斯俏娇娃》。

1384
01:04:09.470 --> 01:04:11.150
When did she kiss Keanu Reeves?
她是什么时候亲到基努·里维斯的？

1385
01:04:11.370 --> 01:04:12.970
In Bill and Ted's second one.
在《比尔和泰德》的第二部里。

1386
01:04:13.430 --> 01:04:13.870
Oh.
哦。

1387
01:04:14.230 --> 01:04:15.610
What about A Walk in the Clouds?
那《云中漫步》呢？

1388
01:04:15.670 --> 01:04:16.530
What about that one?
那部怎么样？

1389
01:04:16.870 --> 01:04:17.790
Yeah, I don't know.
是啊，我不知道。

1390
01:04:17.990 --> 01:04:18.690
I don't know.
我不知道。

1391
01:04:18.770 --> 01:04:20.870
I mean, we have a lot to do.
我是说，我们要做的功课还很多。

1392
01:04:21.090 --> 01:04:23.710
Don't get me started on The Matrix, one of my favorite movies ever.
别让我开始聊《黑客帝国》，那是我最喜欢的电影之一。

1393
01:04:23.930 --> 01:04:27.350
Well, I don't need to rewatch those because I've seen them so many times.
嗯，我不需要重温那些，因为我已经看过太多遍了。

1394
01:04:27.350 --> 01:04:29.690
But I will because I want to.
但我还是会重温的，因为我想看。

1395
01:04:29.910 --> 01:04:30.990
There is no spoon.
勺子是不存在的。

1396
01:04:32.070 --> 01:04:32.590
Yeah.
没错。

1397
01:04:33.510 --> 01:04:34.790
Oh, I'm so excited.
哦，我太兴奋了。

1398
01:04:34.990 --> 01:04:39.950
I had no idea you went down that rabbit hole.
我没想到你竟然掉进了这个坑里。

1399
01:04:40.230 --> 01:04:40.570
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1400
01:04:40.650 --> 01:04:41.790
They play football on the beach.
他们在沙滩上踢橄榄球。

1401
01:04:41.850 --> 01:04:42.530
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1402
01:04:43.150 --> 01:04:43.530
All right.
好吧。

1403
01:04:43.690 --> 01:04:45.830
So the guys, eventually they get to New York.
所以他们最终到了纽约。

1404
01:04:45.830 --> 01:04:47.470
They get to Dunder Mifflin.
他们到了邓德·米夫林公司。

1405
01:04:47.650 --> 01:04:50.150
And we find Michael sitting in the lobby.
然后我们发现迈克尔坐在大厅里。

1406
01:04:50.430 --> 01:04:53.670
And he looks over to the woman sitting next to him.
他看向坐在他旁边的那个女人。

1407
01:04:54.190 --> 01:04:57.270
And she is wearing the same suit.
她穿着同样的套装。

1408
01:04:58.170 --> 01:05:04.610
You know, Jenna, I looked up how many times does Michael Scott wear women's clothing by accident.
你知道吗，珍娜，我查了一下迈克尔·斯科特到底有多少次不小心穿了女装。

1409
01:05:05.450 --> 01:05:07.270
This is going to be a recurring thing.
这会成为一个反复出现的梗。

1410
01:05:07.810 --> 01:05:08.850
It is?
是吗？

1411
01:05:09.330 --> 01:05:09.910
Yes.
是的。

1412
01:05:10.170 --> 01:05:11.430
Do I not remember this?
我不记得了吗？

1413
01:05:11.650 --> 01:05:12.130
Okay.
好吧。

1414
01:05:12.130 --> 01:05:15.910
In launch party, he has on a shirt that's way too tight.
在《发布会》那一集里，他穿了一件紧得离谱的衬衫。

1415
01:05:16.030 --> 01:05:18.930
And the consensus is that it was probably a woman's shirt.
大家一致认为那很可能是一件女式衬衫。

1416
01:05:19.110 --> 01:05:19.470
Okay.
好吧。

1417
01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:25.970
And then in nepotism, Erin mentions that the pants Michael had, that she had to return to Talbot's or something.
然后在《裙带关系》那一集里，艾琳提到迈克尔穿的那条裤子，她不得不退回塔博特百货之类的店里。

1418
01:05:25.970 --> 01:05:30.710
So clearly, he's bought some women's suits repeatedly.
所以很明显，他多次买过女式套装。

1419
01:05:31.210 --> 01:05:33.790
And he says he won't make that mistake again.
而且他说他不会再犯同样的错误了。

1420
01:05:34.350 --> 01:05:35.770
Well, we got some mail.
好吧，我们收到了一些邮件。

1421
01:05:36.010 --> 01:05:44.750
We had some questions from Maruna T., Brianna K., Megan S., Rachel Hayes, and Dan Salomon.
我们收到了一些来自Maruna T.、Brianna K.、Megan S.、Rachel Hayes和Dan Salomon的问题。

1422
01:05:44.970 --> 01:05:52.970
They said, was Steve really wearing a woman's suit or was it custom made for him?
他们问，史蒂夫当时是真的穿了女式套装，还是专门为他定制的？

1423
01:05:53.690 --> 01:05:57.930
So, Ange, I reached out to Carrie Bennett, our wardrobe designer.
所以，安吉，我联系了我们的服装设计师卡莉·贝内特。

1424
01:05:58.790 --> 01:05:59.110
Awesome.
太棒了。

1425
01:05:59.430 --> 01:06:00.830
Here is what she told me.
这是她告诉我的。

1426
01:06:00.950 --> 01:06:04.110
She said it really was a lady's suit.
她说那确实是一套女装。

1427
01:06:05.050 --> 01:06:12.630
She did not have time to sew something from scratch because they would have had to also sew a matching suit for the woman in the lobby.
她没时间从头缝制，因为他们还得为大厅里的那个女人缝制一套一模一样的。

1428
01:06:13.350 --> 01:06:14.690
So here's what she did.
所以她是这么做的。

1429
01:06:15.330 --> 01:06:25.210
She said the first thing she did was try to find a woman's suit that would fit Steve and then hope that she could buy an identical one to fit the woman.
她说她做的第一件事就是试着找一套能穿在史蒂夫身上的女装，然后希望能买到一套一模一样的给那个女人穿。

1430
01:06:25.210 --> 01:06:32.610
So she went to stores with a measuring tape looking for a jacket and pants that would fit Steve's measurements.
于是她带着卷尺去商店，寻找符合史蒂夫尺寸的夹克和裤子。

1431
01:06:32.870 --> 01:06:41.430
But also, she said it had to look masculine enough that it would be plausible that Michael would be confused enough to buy it from a bargain bin.
但她也说，这衣服必须看起来足够男性化，这样迈克尔才会糊涂到从特价区买下它，这在逻辑上才说得通。

1432
01:06:42.270 --> 01:06:42.530
Right.
没错。

1433
01:06:43.290 --> 01:06:55.350
She said that Steve was always so wonderful and generous with his time in the fittings and that oftentimes he would learn about a plot point for a future episode from her.
她说史蒂夫在试装时总是非常配合，慷慨地贡献自己的时间，而且他经常从她那里提前得知未来剧集的剧情点。

1434
01:06:55.590 --> 01:06:57.450
And this was one of those times.
这次就是其中之一。

1435
01:06:57.690 --> 01:07:05.470
She said he walked into a fitting and she was like, so today I'm going to need you to try on all of these women's suits.
她说他走进试衣间，她就说，今天我需要你试穿所有这些女式套装。

1436
01:07:06.090 --> 01:07:07.950
And Steve was like, for why?
史蒂夫就问，为什么？

1437
01:07:07.950 --> 01:07:14.310
And she was like, well, let me tell you, there's going to be an episode next week where this happens.
她说，好吧，我告诉你，下周会有一集发生这样的事。

1438
01:07:14.510 --> 01:07:20.470
Because, you know, they would give the crew these scripts a couple of weeks in advance so they could prepare.
因为你知道，他们会提前几周把剧本给剧组人员，这样他们才能做好准备。

1439
01:07:20.530 --> 01:07:25.530
But the actors, we would only get them, what, five days before we started shooting?
但我们演员通常只在开拍前五天左右才能拿到剧本，对吧？

1440
01:07:26.250 --> 01:07:27.710
Sometimes the day of, Jenna.
有时候是当天，珍娜。

1441
01:07:28.030 --> 01:07:32.830
Sometimes we would get them like an hour before the lunch table read.
有时候我们在午餐剧本围读前一小时才拿到。

1442
01:07:32.990 --> 01:07:36.310
It depended on what kind of turnaround and how long the script was taking.
这取决于周转情况以及剧本创作花了多长时间。

1443
01:07:36.310 --> 01:07:40.750
And I learned about storylines many times in wardrobe.
我很多次都是在服装间得知剧情走向的。

1444
01:07:41.030 --> 01:07:42.070
I totally relate to that.
我完全感同身受。

1445
01:07:42.250 --> 01:07:48.370
I remember learning about Dwight and Angela's wedding because I was going to need to be fitted for a wedding dress.
我记得我是因为需要试穿婚纱，才得知德怀特和安吉拉要结婚的消息。

1446
01:07:48.990 --> 01:07:54.870
Jenna, do you realize that this is the first time we meet Hunter?
珍娜，你意识到这是我们第一次见到亨特吗？

1447
01:07:55.730 --> 01:07:56.310
Yes.
是的。

1448
01:07:56.790 --> 01:07:58.710
Played by Nicholas D'Agosto.
由尼古拉斯·达戈斯托饰演。

1449
01:07:59.050 --> 01:08:01.930
And Michael's like, you didn't tell me you hired James Van Der Beek.
迈克尔说，你没告诉我你雇了詹姆斯·范德比克。

1450
01:08:03.390 --> 01:08:06.690
You know, Angela, this guy has a very extensive resume.
你知道吗，安吉拉，这家伙的履历非常丰富。

1451
01:08:06.970 --> 01:08:12.390
I looked him up, but he was in the movie Election with Reese Witherspoon and Matthew Broderick.
我查过他了，但他演过瑞茜·威瑟斯彭和马修·布罗德里克主演的电影《校园风云》。

1452
01:08:12.490 --> 01:08:13.490
I love that movie.
我喜欢那部电影。

1453
01:08:13.950 --> 01:08:14.410
Yes.
是啊。

1454
01:08:14.630 --> 01:08:17.070
He has starred in Gotham and Trial and Error.
他主演过《哥谭》和《律政急先锋》。

1455
01:08:18.210 --> 01:08:25.410
But I was very excited because he is the lead of Final Destination 5.
但我当时特别兴奋，因为他是《死神来了5》的主角。

1456
01:08:26.030 --> 01:08:29.550
And I'm a huge fan of the Final Destination movies.
而且我是《死神来了》系列的超级粉丝。

1457
01:08:29.950 --> 01:08:31.670
I've never seen one of them.
我一部都没看过。

1458
01:08:32.110 --> 01:08:32.390
What?
什么？

1459
01:08:33.150 --> 01:08:35.050
Well, you hadn't seen Speed.
好吧，你之前也没看过《生死时速》。

1460
01:08:35.050 --> 01:08:35.990
Come on.
得了吧。

1461
01:08:36.110 --> 01:08:37.090
I've seen Speed.
我看过《生死时速》。

1462
01:08:37.090 --> 01:08:39.030
I just hadn't seen Speed in a while.
我只是有一阵子没看了。

1463
01:08:39.490 --> 01:08:40.710
Had you seen Point Break?
你看过《惊爆点》吗？

1464
01:08:41.090 --> 01:08:43.110
Of course I've seen Point Break.
我当然看过《惊爆点》。

1465
01:08:43.330 --> 01:08:47.190
It came out in 1991 when I was a senior in high school.
它1991年上映的时候，我正好上高三。

1466
01:08:47.450 --> 01:08:48.590
Of course I saw it.
我当然看过。

1467
01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:52.390
Every girl who was 17 years old saw Point Break.
每个17岁的女孩都看过《惊爆点》。

1468
01:08:52.390 --> 01:08:54.770
Okay, I haven't seen Final Destination.
好吧，我没看过《死神来了》。

1469
01:08:55.050 --> 01:08:56.190
Is it a scary movie?
那是恐怖片吗？

1470
01:08:56.450 --> 01:08:59.830
Do they have to get somewhere and if they don't get there, they die or something?
是不是他们必须去某个地方，如果没赶到就会死之类的？

1471
01:08:59.830 --> 01:09:01.250
It's their Final Destination?
这就是他们的“死神来了”？

1472
01:09:01.590 --> 01:09:02.790
Here's what happens.
剧情是这样的。

1473
01:09:03.010 --> 01:09:05.370
Everyone starts the same but different.
每一部的开头都大同小异。

1474
01:09:05.730 --> 01:09:07.450
There's a major catastrophe.
会发生一场重大灾难。

1475
01:09:07.830 --> 01:09:10.490
For example, in Final Destination 5,
比如在《死神来了5》里，

1476
01:09:12.070 --> 01:09:16.950
they are supposed to take a bus over a bridge.
他们本该坐大巴过桥。

1477
01:09:17.470 --> 01:09:18.330
Who's they?
他们是谁？

1478
01:09:18.590 --> 01:09:20.370
Like a group of kids.
就是一群孩子。

1479
01:09:20.370 --> 01:09:25.330
Like it's always like a group of teenagers are traveling somewhere by plane or bus
通常都是一群青少年坐飞机或大巴去某地旅行，

1480
01:09:25.330 --> 01:09:30.170
or maybe on the highway and like a major accident happens and they're all killed.
或者在高速公路上，然后发生重大事故，他们全都死了。

1481
01:09:30.870 --> 01:09:31.390
Asteroid.
小行星撞击？

1482
01:09:31.570 --> 01:09:32.290
Something like that?
是那种吗？

1483
01:09:32.810 --> 01:09:35.090
No, it's not science fiction, Angela.
不，安吉拉，那不是科幻片。

1484
01:09:35.250 --> 01:09:35.850
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1485
01:09:35.970 --> 01:09:37.990
There's no asteroid that falls from the sky.
没有小行星从天而降。

1486
01:09:38.330 --> 01:09:38.650
Okay.
好吧。

1487
01:09:39.150 --> 01:09:39.630
Okay.
好吧。

1488
01:09:39.630 --> 01:09:43.850
It's always like a series of little things that lead to a giant calamity.
通常是一连串小事引发了巨大的灾难。

1489
01:09:43.850 --> 01:09:49.450
So like someone's tire bursts and then the car spins and then that hits a truck and then
比如某人的轮胎爆了，车子打滑撞上一辆卡车，然后

1490
01:09:49.450 --> 01:09:53.490
things fall off the truck and hit another truck and then something slams into something and
卡车上的东西掉下来撞上另一辆卡车，接着什么东西又撞上了什么，

1491
01:09:53.490 --> 01:09:55.930
then the whole bridge ends up collapsing, right?
最后整座桥就塌了，对吧？

1492
01:09:56.050 --> 01:09:58.610
And they're trapped on the bus hanging from the bridge or something?
然后他们被困在挂在桥上的大巴里之类的？

1493
01:09:58.810 --> 01:09:59.130
No, they're dead.
不，他们死了。

1494
01:09:59.310 --> 01:10:00.130
They all die.
他们全都死了。

1495
01:10:00.550 --> 01:10:01.290
Oh, oh.
哦，噢。

1496
01:10:01.470 --> 01:10:02.610
Then how do you have a movie?
那电影还怎么演？

1497
01:10:02.610 --> 01:10:03.130
Exactly.
问得好。

1498
01:10:03.790 --> 01:10:10.150
Every movie opens up with like a giant disaster moment and then it rewinds and you realize
每部电影开场都是一场巨大的灾难，然后倒叙，你才意识到

1499
01:10:10.150 --> 01:10:15.430
that it's a person's premonition of what's about to happen and that person freaks out
那是某人的预知梦，预见到了即将发生的事，那个人吓坏了，

1500
01:10:15.430 --> 01:10:16.930
and says, everybody get off the bus.
然后大喊，让所有人下车。

1501
01:10:17.070 --> 01:10:17.730
We're all going to die.
我们都要死了。

1502
01:10:17.870 --> 01:10:18.610
We're all going to die.
我们都要死了。

1503
01:10:18.830 --> 01:10:23.430
And he convinces everyone to get off the bus and they think he's crazy and they get off
然后他劝说所有人下车，大家都觉得他疯了，但还是下了车，

1504
01:10:23.430 --> 01:10:26.890
the bus and then everything happens as they envisioned it.
接着一切正如他预见的那样发生了。

1505
01:10:27.050 --> 01:10:30.710
But they live because of the person's weird premonition, right?
但他们因为那个人的奇怪预感活了下来，对吧？

1506
01:10:31.170 --> 01:10:31.550
Okay.
好吧。

1507
01:10:31.550 --> 01:10:33.470
But here's the problem, Angela.
但问题在于，安吉拉。

1508
01:10:33.970 --> 01:10:35.350
Do they all die anyway?
他们最终还是会死吗？

1509
01:10:35.730 --> 01:10:38.870
They were meant to die on that bus and they've cheated death.
他们注定要死在那辆车上，但他们骗过了死神。

1510
01:10:39.070 --> 01:10:43.490
And so death is now going to come for them slowly, one by one, in the order that they
所以死神现在要一个个慢慢地来找他们，按照他们

1511
01:10:43.490 --> 01:10:44.590
would have died in the accident.
本该在事故中死去的顺序。

1512
01:10:45.190 --> 01:10:46.650
Oh, okay.
噢，好吧。

1513
01:10:47.130 --> 01:10:47.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1514
01:10:47.730 --> 01:10:51.210
It's the same plot every time, but they're great.
每次剧情都一样，但电影真的很棒。

1515
01:10:51.650 --> 01:10:53.370
It sounds really stressful.
听起来压力好大。

1516
01:10:53.830 --> 01:10:55.530
It, it, it, I like movies.
它，它，它，我喜欢电影。

1517
01:10:55.810 --> 01:10:56.770
I, I like it.
我，我喜欢它。

1518
01:10:56.850 --> 01:10:57.550
They relax me.
它们让我放松。

1519
01:10:57.970 --> 01:11:01.050
And, um, I shouldn't say they relax me.
而且，嗯，我不该说它们让我放松。

1520
01:11:01.230 --> 01:11:01.430
No.
不。

1521
01:11:01.550 --> 01:11:03.030
I think they do, Jenna.
我觉得它们确实让你放松，珍娜。

1522
01:11:03.410 --> 01:11:10.510
I think they do because I think I love you, but you will play out the worst case scenario
我觉得是这样，因为我觉得我了解你，你会预想每种情况

1523
01:11:10.510 --> 01:11:12.410
of every situation.
最坏的结果。

1524
01:11:12.630 --> 01:11:12.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1525
01:11:13.390 --> 01:11:14.710
To sort of prepare yourself.
算是为了让自己有所准备。

1526
01:11:14.910 --> 01:11:15.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1527
01:11:15.170 --> 01:11:19.990
So I think movies like this are all horrible worst case scenarios.
所以我认为像这样的电影都是关于各种可怕的最坏情况。

1528
01:11:19.990 --> 01:11:24.070
And in your mind, you're like, oh yeah, I, I would, I would think about that.
而在你脑海里，你会想，哦对，我，我也会那样想。

1529
01:11:24.230 --> 01:11:25.350
I can relate to that.
我能感同身受。

1530
01:11:25.610 --> 01:11:25.830
Yes.
是的。

1531
01:11:25.970 --> 01:11:27.190
Angela, thank you for saying this.
安吉拉，谢谢你这么说。

1532
01:11:27.430 --> 01:11:35.390
I found uncut gems very, I don't want to say soothing, but I just want to say that
我觉得《原钻》非常，我不想说它是治愈的，但我只是想说

1533
01:11:35.390 --> 01:11:41.030
my brain operates on that level of stress and anxiety all the time.
我的大脑一直处于那种压力和焦虑的水平。

1534
01:11:41.410 --> 01:11:47.090
So when I see it depicted, it's sort of, it's like it cancels it out.
所以当我看到它被表现出来时，它就像是，它抵消了那种感觉。

1535
01:11:47.110 --> 01:11:51.470
And I feel like, oh, finally someone's meeting me where I am.
我觉得，噢，终于有人能理解我的处境了。

1536
01:11:51.850 --> 01:11:52.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1537
01:11:52.510 --> 01:11:53.290
You feel seen.
你感到被理解了。

1538
01:11:53.510 --> 01:11:54.490
I think you feel seen.
我觉得你是感到被理解了。

1539
01:11:54.490 --> 01:11:54.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1540
01:11:55.170 --> 01:12:00.390
So I, whereas I know like you or Lee watch a movie like that and you're like, I can't
所以，虽然我知道像你或者李看那样的电影时，你会觉得，我受不了

1541
01:12:00.390 --> 01:12:01.790
handle this.
这个。

1542
01:12:02.050 --> 01:12:03.530
I can't do this.
我做不到。

1543
01:12:03.750 --> 01:12:04.030
Right.
没错。

1544
01:12:04.070 --> 01:12:06.050
That's not, that's not recreation for me.
那对我来说不是娱乐。

1545
01:12:06.150 --> 01:12:07.890
I don't want to feel like that in my free time.
我不想在空闲时间有那种感觉。

1546
01:12:08.010 --> 01:12:09.710
I want to watch Pride and Prejudice.
我想看《傲慢与偏见》。

1547
01:12:09.910 --> 01:12:14.210
I want to watch Keira Knightley say, Mr. Darcy, Mr. Darcy.
我想看凯拉·奈特莉说，达西先生，达西先生。

1548
01:12:14.210 --> 01:12:14.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1549
01:12:15.290 --> 01:12:15.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1550
01:12:17.010 --> 01:12:21.790
Well, anyway, that was a little bit of a tangent, but I just want you to know that's Hunter.
总之，刚才有点跑题了，但我只是想让你知道那就是亨特。

1551
01:12:22.150 --> 01:12:25.390
So now Roy is coming to collect his final paycheck.
所以现在罗伊要来领他最后一份工资了。

1552
01:12:25.690 --> 01:12:27.710
You know, Angela must be very excited.
你知道，安吉拉肯定很兴奋。

1553
01:12:28.470 --> 01:12:29.910
She's so thrilled now.
她现在激动坏了。

1554
01:12:30.350 --> 01:12:32.330
Roy and Dwight are in the same room.
罗伊和德怀特在同一个房间里。

1555
01:12:32.530 --> 01:12:33.770
Oh, anything could happen.
哦，什么事都可能发生。

1556
01:12:34.330 --> 01:12:34.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1557
01:12:36.250 --> 01:12:42.630
And there's a moment where Kevin runs out and he goes, Jim, Roy, look out.
然后有个瞬间，凯文跑出来喊道：吉姆，罗伊，小心。

1558
01:12:42.850 --> 01:12:43.990
Like so delayed.
反应太迟钝了。

1559
01:12:44.210 --> 01:12:44.770
It's too late.
太晚了。

1560
01:12:44.950 --> 01:12:47.570
He's pointing a Twizzler.
他手里指着一条扭扭糖。

1561
01:12:47.790 --> 01:12:48.790
Is that what it is?
那是扭扭糖吗？

1562
01:12:49.030 --> 01:12:50.630
It's a Twizzler or a Red Vine.
是扭扭糖或者红藤糖。

1563
01:12:50.830 --> 01:12:52.870
We had a big, big container of them.
我们当时有一大桶那种糖。

1564
01:12:52.990 --> 01:12:54.390
Remember in the kitchen?
还记得在厨房里吗？

1565
01:12:54.690 --> 01:12:54.990
Oh yeah.
哦，记得。

1566
01:12:55.110 --> 01:12:55.870
They were Red Vines.
那是红藤糖。

1567
01:12:56.090 --> 01:13:00.790
I remember I got into a big debate on set about, about the Red Vines container.
我记得在片场时，我还因为那个红藤糖桶引发了一场大争论。

1568
01:13:01.230 --> 01:13:01.450
Yes.
